        "title": "Restore Qwen3 MoE component registration",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Config retains its model_classes argument verbatim. Model.from_config defaults component to \"text\", checks membership, then invokes the selected class with config and forwarded kwargs. The patch repairs the producer rather than adding a bare-class compatibility branch to these consumers.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9bb71336784143b6812caa9e0327327f",
              "call_64b8f3a954b34fb6a8f8bc37c066d280",
              "call_39cd9b8a2dca4a6da47fa26e21f1dc3f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The selected Qwen3MoeModel constructor remains unchanged: it assembles embeddings, attention and sparse-expert transformer blocks, final normalization and the output head, and enables all-expert calibration. The change repairs access to that constructor, not its numerical computation.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_63b78b662a92465bae992a9684af6d96",
              "call_39cd9b8a2dca4a6da47fa26e21f1dc3f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A bounded Python transcription produced TypeError for bare-class membership and AttributeError for bare-class .items(); the text dictionary selected the stand-in constructor and collected an empty additional-tensor result. This checks the interface mechanism, not repository execution.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_0b70f52e1c144cf0b90fe4b68ea89ed8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The inspected config.json files for Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B, Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-FP8 and Qwen/Qwen3-235B-A22B-GPTQ-Int4 each declare Qwen3MoeForCausalLM, matching Qwen3MoeConfig.arch_string. The same repaired text-component mapping applies to each; the patch changes no dimensions or configuration defaults.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
